w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-03T21:21:51Z","updated_at":"2025-05-03T21:22:31Z","body":"For the longest time I kept suspecting that [the Spanish localization has been extremely shoddy](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/translation?msg=pFZrNuRmNR7yf6XKx), but as a non-native speaker I cannot confirm it.\n\nOn Weblate, the localization string is [right here](https://hosted.weblate.org/translate/godot-engine/godot-properties/es/?checksum=595fb04ff5113fa1). So all @Torguen would have to do, if they want, is to contribute and change it themselves.\n\nRegardless, issues with localization of other languages shouldn't be tracked here, or at all, I believe?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2848813852/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2849031565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106035#issuecomment-2849031565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106035","id":2849031565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6p0MWN","user":{"login":"PabloDevGit","id":19652075,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjUyMDc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19652075?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit","html_url":"https://github.com/PabloDevGit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-04T06:11:26Z","updated_at":"2025-05-04T06:11:26Z","body":"I thought the use of integers (naturals in the Spanish translation) would also apply to the + and - zoom buttons, but it seems it's only applied when using the mouse wheel to zoom. Zoom values with the mouse wheel go 100 -> 200 -> 300 in steps of 100.\n\nIf that's the case, then I was wrong. But if integer values are also supposed to apply to the + and - zoom buttons, then there's a bug.\n\n\nBut integers also include 25, 50, 45, etc... that is, anything that is not fractional is an integer.\nSo why does the zoom increase in steps of 100 (which is very large) instead of 25, for example? Like 100 – 125 - 150, etc.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2849031565/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocke